WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.428
ReciReflect is a recipe recommender built for research on transparent recommendation.

00:00:05.428 --> 00:00:12.419
Every score can be opened, every step of its agent is visible, and nothing about your goal changes until you agree.

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:18.654
To see how it works, we will follow Sara, a fictional participant in a sample study.

00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:23.183
She wants to eat green and healthy food, but she also has a very busy week.

00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:28.074
Let's see what happens when what she says and what she does start to drift apart.

00:00:29.003 --> 00:00:33.121
Sara signs in with the account her study administrator created for her.

00:00:33.426 --> 00:00:35.143
Setup begins with safety.

00:00:35.143 --> 00:00:36.927
Sara has a peanut allergy.

00:00:36.927 --> 00:00:41.870
Allergies and diets are strict rules, applied before anything is ranked.

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:44.461
Next come her tastes.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:50.407
Ingredients and cuisines are preferences, so they only shape how well a dish matches her taste.

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:56.906
She chooses a health goal, which decides how nutrients are weighted inside her healthiness score.

00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:02.489
A few dishes she already likes can give the taste model a starting point.

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:04.060
She can skip this for now.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:07.928
Then the most important step: her values.

00:01:07.928 --> 00:01:11.614
Sara says sustainability matters most, at fifty percent.

00:01:11.614 --> 00:01:15.498
Healthiness gets thirty five, and convenience only fifteen.

00:01:15.498 --> 00:01:17.341
This becomes her saved goal.

00:01:17.341 --> 00:01:21.357
Taste keeps a fixed share, and is learned from her reactions.

00:01:28.345 --> 00:01:29.445
This is Discover.

00:01:29.445 --> 00:01:32.293
Five dishes are ranked by Sara's own values.

00:01:32.293 --> 00:01:41.095
Each card shows a health grade from A to E, its sustainability and convenience scores, and the reason for the suggestion in plain words.

00:01:41.654 --> 00:01:43.430
Nothing here is a black box.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:53.070
How it's scored opens the full calculation: each criterion, its weight, and its contribution to the final score, right down to the individual nutrients.

00:01:56.077 --> 00:01:58.318
The assistant sits beside every page.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:03.456
Sara asks why the first dish is on top, and she can open every step it took to answer.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:15.046
A language model can interpret the message and phrase the reply, but the ranking and the facts always come from a deterministic engine, and any wording the evidence does not support is rejected.

00:02:15.608 --> 00:02:16.977
She can also explore.

00:02:16.977 --> 00:02:19.649
What if she cared more about convenience?

00:02:19.649 --> 00:02:23.430
This is only a preview, showing how the list would change.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.538
Nothing is saved.

00:02:29.325 --> 00:02:30.968
Now her busy week begins.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:36.291
Sara keeps choosing the simplest dish, and tells the app why: it is easy to make.

00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:40.563
The app asks whether that reason is lasting, or only about today.

00:02:40.563 --> 00:02:42.075
She says it is lasting.

00:02:42.281 --> 00:02:46.905
She also turns down the most involved dish, because it has too many ingredients.

00:02:47.142 --> 00:02:51.389
The panel we have added at the bottom of the screen is only for this video.

00:02:51.389 --> 00:02:59.429
It shows the live numbers from the app: the convenience weight in Sara's saved goal, the weight her choices suggest, and the gap between them.

00:02:59.988 --> 00:03:03.508
After every reaction, the supervisor compares the two.

00:03:03.508 --> 00:03:06.507
It acts only when the gap crosses a threshold.

00:03:06.507 --> 00:03:11.787
While the gap is small, it stays quiet, and Sara simply gets her recommendations.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:17.288
There it is.

00:03:17.288 --> 00:03:24.302
The gap has passed zero point one zero, with at least three informative reactions since her goal was saved.

00:03:24.302 --> 00:03:27.973
That is the first threshold, so the supervisor steps in.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.611
But only with a question.

00:03:29.916 --> 00:03:34.050
When her values pull in different directions, which usually wins?

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:37.674
It explains what it noticed and what each answer will do.

00:03:37.674 --> 00:03:40.790
Sara could also say only today, or keep her goal.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.525
None of these options edits her saved goal.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.719
Sara answers that convenience usually wins.

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:52.678
That updates what has been learned about her, and her saved goal stays exactly as it was.

00:03:54.388 --> 00:03:56.273
She carries on through the week.

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:59.514
The gap keeps growing, but the supervisor does not nag.

00:03:59.514 --> 00:04:04.875
After an answer, it waits for six more feedback events before raising the same topic again.

00:04:15.984 --> 00:04:18.125
Now the second threshold is reached.

00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:25.262
The gap is above zero point one five, with at least six informative reactions behind it, and the waiting period is over.

00:04:25.262 --> 00:04:28.235
The evidence is strong enough for a goal proposal.

00:04:28.557 --> 00:04:36.193
The supervisor shows her saved weight, the weight her choices suggest, and a change that moves it halfway between the two.

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:42.578
Whenever a change would alter her top five, the card also names the recipes that would enter or leave.

00:04:42.578 --> 00:04:47.461
She can update her goal, use the change only today, or keep her goal as it is.

00:04:47.776 --> 00:04:49.314
The decision is Sara's.

00:04:49.314 --> 00:04:52.458
She accepts, and only now does her goal change.

00:04:57.177 --> 00:04:59.097
The earlier goal is not lost.

00:04:59.097 --> 00:05:04.262
Every goal is kept as a version, and Sara can restore any of them at any time.

00:05:04.821 --> 00:05:12.975
Insights puts it side by side: what Sara said she values, next to what her choices show, with the evidence behind every change.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:19.606
Activity keeps the full record: every reaction she made, and every decision the supervisor reached.

00:05:20.122 --> 00:05:27.817
And this is the knowledge graph the supervisor draws its evidence from, connecting Sara to her goals, her choices, and her reasons.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.732
Now let's switch sides.

00:05:34.732 --> 00:05:38.479
A study administrator signs in and opens the Config page.

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:44.461
Everything we have just seen is controlled here, and stored in a single configuration file.

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:46.101
Settings comes first.

00:05:46.101 --> 00:05:53.417
The language model can run locally through Ollama, through any OpenAI compatible service, or through the Claude API.

00:05:53.417 --> 00:06:00.986
ReciReflect also works with no model at all, using built-in rules and templates, which is how this walkthrough was recorded.

00:06:01.546 --> 00:06:11.639
Further down are the dataset, the ranking options, such as how many dishes are reserved for discovery, and the meal cycle: how many days and meals a study runs for.

00:06:12.195 --> 00:06:16.523
This is the Supervisor section, with the thresholds we just watched.

00:06:16.523 --> 00:06:20.787
A gap of zero point one zero after three events prompts a question.

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:24.924
A gap of zero point one five after six events prompts a proposal.

00:06:24.924 --> 00:06:28.425
And six events of cooldown separate repeated questions.

00:06:28.425 --> 00:06:31.989
Lower these numbers and the supervisor speaks up sooner.

00:06:31.989 --> 00:06:34.917
Raise them and it waits for stronger evidence.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:39.135
Criteria and interactions defines what people weigh.

00:06:39.135 --> 00:06:49.719
Healthiness, sustainability and convenience can be renamed or switched off, and any numeric field in your dataset, such as price, can become a new criterion.

00:06:49.719 --> 00:06:55.045
This tab also sets the feedback reasons, and how strongly each reaction counts.

00:06:55.602 --> 00:07:01.227
Access roles is a matrix of features by role, which is how a study compares conditions.

00:07:01.227 --> 00:07:06.141
One group can get full transparency while another sees only a baseline list.

00:07:06.141 --> 00:07:10.861
These rules are enforced on the server, not just hidden in the interface.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.802
Users and study creates the population.

00:07:13.802 --> 00:07:20.036
Choose the number of participants and how they split across roles, and ReciReflect generates the accounts.

00:07:20.593 --> 00:07:27.482
Export produces one standard record per user, as JSON or as CSV tables, ready for analysis.

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:34.870
All of these settings live in one configuration file, so a study's setup can be saved, shared and repeated.

00:07:36.032 --> 00:07:37.281
That is ReciReflect.

00:07:37.281 --> 00:07:39.836
The agent manages the learning process.

00:07:39.836 --> 00:07:41.539
It does not pick the food.

00:07:41.539 --> 00:07:47.566
Ranking stays auditable, the evidence stays visible, and the decisions stay with the person.
